-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §6.1, R-T3: `BREACH BY` given a list literal
-- with nobody in it is refused when the file is CHECKED — a breach blames at
-- least one party, and a literal is decidable here. Both spellings of the
-- literal are caught; a computed list that turns out empty is refused when
-- the rule runs instead (ok/every/run-blame.l4, `blame nobody`).

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF deliver

`by empty` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 LEST BREACH BY EMPTY

`by list of nothing` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 LEST BREACH BY (LIST)
